WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.960
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.280
So this is Tokyo Station!

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.510
It's just like on TV!

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.600
My goodness, look at all these people.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.100
Okay, so I just need to change trains at...

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.190
I better make sure I don't take the wrong train.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:47.610
Huh?

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.040
Th-thief!

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.190
How dare you lay your hands on someone else's things?

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.190
Here. Are you all right?

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.600
Oh, thank you so much.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.360
<i>She's so pretty...</i>

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.960
<i>She's got that refined metropolitan look to her.</i>

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.780
<i>So cool and beautiful and...</i>

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.440
You be careful, okay?

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.650
Thank you so, so much!

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.220
Buh-bye now.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:26.230
<i>I guess there are nice people in Tokyo after all.</i>

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:32.580
<i>Dad, Mom, I think I'm going to be quite all right here!</i>

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.120
Thank you for riding with...

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.780
<i>Where am I...?</i>

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.800
<i>Dad, Mom,</i>

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:55.820
<i> I don't think I'm going to be all right at all here...
Dad, Mom,</i>

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.820
<i> I don't think I'm going to be all right at all here...</i>

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.390
Phew I made it!

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.890
Good thing I took the earlier shinkansen.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.360
If I had shown up late...

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.560
You good for nothing country bumpkin!

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.310
Aaaah! A demonic Tokyoite!
You good for nothing country bumpkin!

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.900
Aaaah! A demonic Tokyoite!

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.150
Sorry for the wait.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.280
Ack! I'm sorry! I'm sorry I ever set foot in Tokyo!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.320
Did I make you wait long?

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.150
Huh...?

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.160
You must be Michiru Amatsuki.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.410
Y-yeah.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.330
I'm Kae Midorikawa.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.660
I'm here to pick you up!

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.170
I'm Amatsuki! Nice to meet you!

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.170
<i>S-so... </i>this<i> is what Tokyoites are like...</i>

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.460
Shall we get going then?

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.440
Okay!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.090
<i>I-I've got my work cut out for me...!</i>

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.140
Wow!

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.180
This is Stella House Haruno.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.640
So this is my new home!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.680
It's a share house just for women.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.650
There are three of us living her including myself.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.310
You're our fourth, Michiru-chan.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.690
<i>Yikes, I'm all nervous all of a sudden.</i>

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.700
Pardon me then...

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.870
From here on this is your house too,
so no need to be shy.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.120
Oh, right...

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.460
I'm... home, then.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.710
Welcome home!

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.710
<i>Th-this is all too much!</i>

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.460
Nao-chan,

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.900
our new roommate is here!

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.260
Not so loud, sheesh...

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.510
Now, now, sit up straight you.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.150
I'm Nao Kiriyama.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.770
Good to meetcha...

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.270
Sorry about that Michiru-chan.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.820
She's been drinking since noon
since she has the day off today.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.140
New roommate?

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.410
We should celebrate!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:46.950
Welcome to Stella House!
We've been looking forward to this!

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.080
Now to celebrate!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.910
By cracking open a Yebisu beer!

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.900
Sheesh, you're really going to keep drinking?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.670
Well, duh!

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.860
We're talking about Yebisu here. Yebisu!

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.420
I was worried you'd have downed them all already.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.630
Oh, no, I would never!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.220
Hmm?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.680
Okay just one.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.600
Then why are there two missing?

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.680
I'll wash the dishes to make up for it!

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.100
Now as way of apology allow me to pour you
a fan-freaking-tastic glass of Yebisu beer!

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.860
Hold that glass for me, would ya?

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.110
L-like this?

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.110
Get ready!

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.610
Here GOES!

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.700
Relax, relax! A good pouring is key!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.620
First we fill it up about half way and then STOP!

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:39.880
Now we let the fizz there settle down
and wait until it's about half foam half beer.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:45.340
Next we pour very carefully making sure
to keep the foam until it's about 90% full.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.900
Then you gotta hold back that desire
to gulp it down and just wait.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.050
Now here's the last part!

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:55.860
Pour the rest in nice and slow
to bring the head to the top.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:01.860
The perfect ratio is 7 to 3 and with that it's ready!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.650
Oh my! It's like something out of a commercial!

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:06.780
Right?

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.660
This is the ideal way to pour
the perfect glass of Yebisu beer.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.540
I call it the three step pour!

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.420
Now then, let's celebrate Michiru Amatsuki
moving in with us here!

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.790
Cheers!

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.440
The foam is so fluffy...!

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.090
Right? Right?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.470
The foam is so fine and the bubbles have settled down.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.310
That's the magic of the three step pour!

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.430
Now Michiru-chan, make sure you eat up!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.270
Chilled tofu is the perfect match for a summer drink.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:41.110
I topped it off with some plum and okra
to make it even more refreshing.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.280
Don't mind if I do!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.340
Oh, that plum accent really stimulates the palate!

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.820
And it looks just as wonderful as it tastes!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.780
And nothing like some beer to wash it down!

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.450
<i>How can she drink that much...?!</i>

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.210
Here's some chopped avocado and tuna
dressed with wasabi soy sauce.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.400
The avocado is so rich it's just perfect with a beer.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.840
That wasabi is just the perfect dose of spicy!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.730
<i>Small dishes like these are what summer is all about.</i>

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.860
<i>The heat can drain your appetite after all!</i>

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.350
<i>How can she eat that much...?!</i>

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.520
Now that you've got your chopsticks warmed up and ready,

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.230
it's time for our main dish.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.110
Shrimp and summer veggie tempura.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:21.940
Bring on the fried goodies!

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.110
Even in this heat you can't help
but crave something deep fried.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.490
No matter how hot...

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.440
Whoa, hang in there Kae!

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.120
I'll crank up the A/C!

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.830
Now nice and hot tempura is fine with salt.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:42.530
But here we dig in with some grated daikon and dipping sauce.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.150
Oh, my! How refreshing!

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.130
Glad to have you back!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:56.670
Oh, that grated daikon is to die for!

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:59.560
And that freshly fried batter is so light and crispy...

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.690
Fried food and beer go hand in hand,

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:01.700
but a premium beer like this would be wasted on anything too heavy.
Fried food and beer go hand in hand,

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:05.800
but a premium beer like this would be wasted on anything too heavy.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.230
Good thinking...

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.780
<i>I guess there's food to match every sort of drink.</i>

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.280
To be honest though Yebisu beer
tastes great no matter what you eat.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.540
<i>How uncouth!</i>

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.540
Hey, by the way,
why did you move out to Tokyo anyway?

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.540
For work! I'm going to be working
sales a startup company.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.190
I'm going to stride through the crowds in my suit.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:31.230
Drink a smoothie every morning.
Eat my own handmade lunch in the afternoon.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:34.300
And finish off the night at a fancy restaurant with a view!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.220
Sales sounds pretty tough, though.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.100
Don't let your quotas drive you crazy.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:39.110
Can you not crush my dreams right from the get go!
Don't let your quotas drive you crazy.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.730
Can you not crush my dreams right from the get go!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.940
What do both of you do, though?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.480
I work in the apparel industry.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.320
I'm a wedding planner.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.740
Oh, wow! Those both sounds so lovely and fun!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.990
Okay what's with the silent treatment?!

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:59.400
You've still got that light of hope... huh, Michiru?

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:03.480
We were like that too, once upon a time.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.090
It's true! We had hopes and dreams!

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:08.090
But...

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.340
before we knew it our dreams were shattered,

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.090
and the hope drained from our eyes...

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.780
Before long,
all we were doing was griping and moaning...

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:21.360
We want nothing but happiness,
but are not spared even the time to seek it out...

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:22.770
N..Nao-san?

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.280
That's life, kid!

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.230
<i>She's seriously crying?</i>

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.650
Then one day while I was trying
to drown my sorrows away...

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.610
Yebisu is so goood!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.480
Grant me your attention.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.240
Who's there?

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:38.490
The label on that bottle you're holding.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.750
Yebisu-sama?!

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:44.360
Yebisu-sama spoke to me.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:46.750
Oh, you poor soul...

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.420
And that very same bottle...

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:51.860
...is right here!

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.010
My lucky Yebisu!

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.590
This little bottle saved you, huh?

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:56.600
Don't look at me like I'm crazy!
This little bottle saved you, huh?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.900
Don't look at me like I'm crazy!

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.770
Go ahead and compare it to this can here!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.270
Hey! There's a fish in the basket on this one!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:10.780
Exactly! It's a super rare special label!
The luckiest Yebisu around!

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.530
Nao-chan you still had that thing?

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.280
It's my most cherished possession!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:19.660
And so yeah, that brought
a spark of happiness back into my life.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:22.660
So you just do your best, okay Michiru?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.790
Lucky Yebisu here, is watching over you!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.370
I'm already quite lucky.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.920
My first time in Tokyo and I meet such friendly people.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.000
Everything about Tokyo is so unfamiliar,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.180
and I was afraid to live alone so I picked this share house.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.260
But that meant I'd have to live with people I've never even met,

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:46.310
so I was worried maybe we wouldn't get along.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.810
Looks like I was worried for nothing, though.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.580
So thank you both again!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.820
No, thank you!
Oh, Michiru!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.320
Welcome to the group.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:05.900
Oh! She's back! My sweet sister!

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.080
Huh? Is our other roommate...

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.460
Yup! She's Nao's little sister.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.170
I'm home.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.500
Makoto!

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.470
Welcome home! Nghh!

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:19.220
Oh!

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.610
You big meanie! Why would you avoid me like that?

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.400
You reek of beer.

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:27.190
U-umm...

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:31.150
I'm Michiru Amatsuki,
the one you helped at Tokyo Station.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.070
Oh, that was you?

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.730
Thank you so much for that!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.740
No, no, nice to meet you for real though.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:42.740
Yeah, you too!

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.620
Hey, now! Why don't you treat me like that?

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.040
Well Makoto-chan is not exactly fond of drunks.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.830
I'm not drunk!

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.060
Michiru! You and Makoto know each other?

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.130
I ran into her at Tokyo Station.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.510
I was so lucky, she really saved me...

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.360
I hope we get along.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:12.150
Nao-chan, how long are you going
to sit there zoning out?

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.230
Look, we were up so late drinking...

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.570
I hope Michiru-chan is okay.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.480
Good morning!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.490
I went and picked up breakfast at the convenience store!

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.580
How is she so lively...?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.250
Are you all right? You don't feel hungover or anything?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.400
Oh, no, I'm fine.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.250
My parents are pretty heavy drinkers you see.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:38.510
Ever since I turned 20,
I've drank at home a lot with them.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:43.070
I'll pick up something for us to drink
on the way home tonight.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.610
<i>Wait, is she a heavier drinker than us?!
Wait, is she a heavier drinker than us?!</i>

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:52.150
<i>This is the start of my new life in Tokyo.</i>

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:54.610
<i>I'm going to make the very best
of my work and home life!</i>

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:02.660
I thought that jingle that plays
at Ebisu station sounded familiar.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.780
Turns out it was from the Yebisu Beer commercial!

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:09.320
Apparently it's the theme song
from the movie "The Third Man."

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:12.150
Tokyo is just so stylish!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.400
Here's to another night! Cheers!
